* JFET Clean Boost — exported from Lutherie
* One JFET in common source with a bypassed source resistor: up to about 20 dB of clean gain.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 100n
JJ1 N3 N2 N4 J_J201
CJ1gs N2 N4 4p
CJ1gd N2 N3 4p
RR1 N2 0 1Meg
RR2 N4 0 680
CC2 N4 0 10u
RR3 VCC_9V N3 6.8k
VVCC1 VCC_9V_src 0 DC 9.0
RVCC1s VCC_9V_src VCC_9V 0.01
CC3 N3 N6 1u
* Level pot 100k A taper at 70%
RVR1a 0 OUT 25.8k
RVR1b OUT N6 74.2k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg

.model J_J201 NJF(Beta=0.001304 Vto=-0.5 Lambda=0.0125)

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata jfet_clean_boost.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end